  "validation": {
    "python_tests": "14 passed; POC CLI baseline and bytecode prevention passed",
    "docker_runtime": "macOS isolated inventory and Compose repeated up passed. Configuration, health, actual image, tmpfs and named volume name differences were checked. External test volumes were preserved.",
    "rust_compiler": "macOS ARM64: 103 Rust tests and registered integration passed. Ubuntu Parallels ARM64: static musl application cross-linked and ran natively. Windows ARM64 NTFS: nine native fixture tests with the earlier qualified source.",
    "html_parse": "passed",
    "agent_integration": "Mac and native Ubuntu Parallels: nine actual CLI cases each using synthetic model replies and a tool stub. On hook error Claude kept the stub from running; Codex and Gemini ran it. Read-only MCP preserved project state.",
    "dockerd_broker": "Rust tree 681be1e passed the macOS isolated live Docker boundary and temporary GUI launchd. Earlier Linux restricted UID/systemd ran with real Docker. Earlier Windows ARM64 native SCM and SID boundary used a fixture pipe.",
    "dashboard": "Current ada5a09: installed macOS API and WebKit at 1060/390 px matched independent Docker counts (7 containers, 8 image IDs, 2 volumes, 0 duplicate groups). Linux and Windows ARM64 and x64 emulation passed loopback dashboard coverage.",
    "release_packages": "Current Rust tree ada5a09 for four local 0.1.1-rc.1 targets. macOS ARM64 matched two independent builds and prior package upgrade, rollback and re-upgrade. Native Linux and Windows ARM64 passed lifecycle. Windows x64 passed cross-link, repeat packaging and Windows ARM64 emulated execution and wrong-host rejection; native x64 remains pending.",
    "windows_qualification": "Current Windows ARM64 and x64 artifacts had matching repeat packages and passed host PE and package checks. Existing Windows ARM64 NTFS passed the actual same-version ARM64 upgrade, dashboard and removal. x64 binaries and dashboard ran emulated, with install and upgrade rejected and ARM64 installation preserved.",
    "release_signature": "macOS ARM64 offline signer handoff, exact archive and manifest verification, rejected responses, publisher-gated local package rejection, and package lifecycle passed. Official signer qualification remains separate.",
    "build_providers": "macOS Cargo, Node, pnpm, Gradle, uv, Go and Playwright ran. Real Next.js 16.4.6 build and loopback response passed with two audited leases. Playwright success/failure and TTL retention were qualified separately.",
    "documentation_traceability": "14 WBS rows, 8 DSG stages, 13 requirement IDs, current four package hashes and local evidence matched. Python 14 and Rust 103 plus registered integration passed.",
    "windows_foundation": "Windows ARM64 MSVC cross-link and nine native NTFS filesystem tests passed on the existing Parallels guest. macOS Python 14 and Rust 98 plus registered integration passed.",
    "buildx_cache": "macOS Rust 102 and live isolated Buildx integration passed. Engine default Buildx totals 208 records, 208 reclaimable, 8 shared, 167 mutable; all preserved. Separate builder qualification remains open.",
    "next_and_compose_health": "macOS Rust 102 and integration passed with the real Next.js 16.4.6 pnpm build, loopback runtime and leases, plus real same-container Compose health rejection and bounded cleanup.",
    "gc_crash_recovery": "macOS Rust 103 and integration passed. Committed GC intent and staged artifact survived an owned child SIGKILL, restored identical identity/SHA-256 with zero deletion and retained exact audit events.",
    "current_macos_qualification": "Rust tree ada5a09: two independent archive builds matched. Installed candidate passed upgrade, rollback, re-upgrade, diagnosis, read-only MCP, WebKit/API with live Docker counts and removal preserving user fixture files.",
    "compose_live_changes": "Existing isolated engine preserved one ID on repeat. Configuration, health, image and tmpfs changes rejected. Matching tmpfs remained unknown. Named volume replacement is covered by synthetic fixtures.",
    "linux_arm64_qualification": "Current 681be1e static musl passed previous archive upgrade, managed success, timeout 124 and lease reacquisition, dashboard and removal in an isolated ARM64 Linux container. Existing Ubuntu Parallels lacked a verified transfer path.",
    "standalone_buildkit": "Linux ARM64 on existing Ubuntu Parallels: product and official BuildKit v0.35.1 matched counts 0 and 4. Wrong PID, wrong client digest and socket symlink were rejected; all cache preserved.",
    "named_volume_reuse": "Real isolated Compose reused identical named volume A and one ID. Replacing A with B rejected the old name and accepted the expected new mount. Read-only, nocopy and both volumes preserved verified.",
    "windows_installer_process_architecture": "Current ada5a09 package: on the existing ARM64 Windows Parallels guest, native ARM64 and emulated x64 portable CPython 3.13.9 each returned exit 1 with the expected host mismatch for x64 install and upgrade. Prefix, existing pointer, installed hashes and fixture user file were preserved. Guest was restored to suspended. x64 operating-system lifecycle awaits a separate environment."
